  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Public Diplomacy in Mexico (EUPOP Mexico III)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;EUPOP Mexico III aims to support the implementation of EU foreign policy objectives by strengthening the EU&apos;s ability to engage meaningfully with selected audiences in third countries (i.e. students/academics, multipliers/influencers, civil society and cultural operators/artists) in order to increase mutual understanding, improve the perception of the EU and of its policies and, ultimately, identify and nurture like-minded allies in bilateral and multilateral cooperation. More specifically, it will a) strengthen EU &#xbf; Mexico engagement on priority areas with the following stakeholder groups, such as Decision-makers (members of congress at federal, state and municipal level, civil servants, diplomats and would-be diplomats, business and industry federations/associations, etc.); Influencers and multipliers (academics, journalists, think tanks, etc.), Civil society actors; Cultural stakeholders and Future leaders; b) Deepen the engagement and exchanges with authorities and civil society actors at Mexican state level; c) Enhance the knowledge and understanding, perception, and attractiveness of the EU among targeted audiences in Mexico;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
